            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0809" n="721" xml:id="pg721"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/2594: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-14T17:00:00-05:00">February 14, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. Your 10, February 10, 5 p.m. You may inform the President that the Department
                    will give immediate consideration to the credit proposal as soon as it is
                    submitted by the Bankers. At the same time you may inquire of the President when
                    the Department may expect to receive the Haitian Government’s proposals for
                    modification of the Treaty of September 3 and urge that they be submitted as
                    soon as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
